WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.140
...started to kind of get back on track, and
we had a conversation about, you know,

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.580
do we actually want to do this?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.480
And it just felt like the right time.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:15.980
So in March of 2012,
we started JM2 Architecture,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.960
and there were probably about
eight clients that we had.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.940
And we got our big break in
April or May, when Amneal

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:30.980
Pharmaceuticals was doing a large
400,000 square foot addition

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:36.180
to their existing facility in Brookhaven,
and John and I were just operating out of a

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.860
bedroom with one computer, one printer,
a little gray buffet table from Home

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:47.500
Depot as our conference room table,
and this project came along, and we

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.300
were under crazy deadlines. It forced us to
work nearly around the clock in the

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:57.820
beginning, because it was a very
high-profile project, and it had

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:03.760
every local official, politician, everybody
wanted to be a part of this. We were a

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.020
lead project. We were adding 750 jobs.
It was a $130 million project, so

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.560
there was a lot of attention on it.
It was a very high-profile project, and for us,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:19.000
right out of the gate, we had to do
everything possible to make it happen.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:23.720
And I'll never forget the construction
manager, the late Jack Hulka, said,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.620
"James, how long is it going to take
you to do site plans?"
